vation","occurredAt":"2024-05-16T15:00:00Z"},"sources":[{"sourceId":"alex-001447","occurredAt":"2024-05-16T15:00:00Z","metadata":{"role":"user","author":"Alex Valdez","localTime":"2024-05-16T11:00:00-04:00"},"label":"Alex Valdez, message 001447","excerpts":["contract requires a source timestamp. The ownership example correctly uses the published `responsible_team` label and `last_verified_at`, without an owner-map ID. Iris also asked whether deploy provenance should expose a customer-stable source event ID or"]}]},{"id":"63b19d25-25a4-80eb-a807-abec79e24b3c","rank":20,"occurredAt":"2025-02-12T15:18:00Z","content":"Iris completed the four-account evaluation using the fixed candidate-scan criteria we defined. Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce passed every criterion: every proposed service has a published owner-map record; the data scan found no renderable deploy event without a tenant-scoped provenance source identifier and source timestamp; every incident-load summary has a source timestamp; stale or missing input renders as explicit unknown; and each pilot configuration includes an operational contact. Each of the other two candidates failed at least one criterion and is deferred. I verified that the monitoring handoff and rollback signals cover the approved external-preview boundary. Hema and Theo authorized Harbor Health and Mosaic Commerce for a read-only 30-day pilot beginning March 10, but customer access does not open today. Every lookup must use the shared authorization wrapper and remain limited to provenance-backed deploy events, published ownership, incident-load summaries with timestamps, and explicit unknown states. The automatic stops are an authorization-wrapper bypass; an adapter call after denial; cross-tenant material; stale or missing input rendered as anything other than unknown; a deploy event without required provenance; unpublished ownership; an incident-load summary without its timestamp; exposure of raw incident text, internal room metadata, or individual comparisons; inferred ownership; fallback internal-only metadata; or loss of read-only enforcement. Any one of those suspends all pilot access until correction and a successful rerun of the affected safety check. Latency and other errors remain monitored but do not independently stop the pilot unless they cause one of those violations. No customer access or app change is requested today.","artifact":{"id":"4cac28d0-9a2e-4a1f-82e1-9d88c5ec7dc0","kind":"source","occurredAt":"2025-02-12T15:18:00Z"},"sources":[{"sourceId":"alex-002396","occurredAt":"2025-02-12T15:18:00Z","metadata":{"role":"user","author":"Alex Valdez","localTime":"2025-02-12T10:18:00-05:00"},"label":"Alex Valdez, message 002396","excerpts":[]}]},{"id":"451099a1-6750-8261-b0cf-4da918b0d074","rank":21,"occurredAt":"2024-06-12T13:35:00Z","content":"Alex Valdez: Product Engineering revised the Lantern fixture so a deploy event is emitted only when all required provenance fields validate together; missing provenance produces an unknown result with a missing_provenance reason and no partial deploy object (outcome).","artifact":{"id":"9c3a624c-758a-48fd-9e70-21ab10ec0670","kind":"observation","occurredAt":"2024-06-12T13:35:00Z"},"sources":[{"sourceId":"alex-001539","occurredAt":"2024-06-12T13:35:00Z","metadata":{"role":"user","author":"Alex Valdez","localTime":"2024-06-12T09:35:00-04:00"},"label":"Alex Valdez, message 001539","excerpts":["Product Engineering revised the Lantern fixture so a deploy event is emitted only when the repository, commit, deploy timestamp, pipeline run identifier, and source timestamp all validate together. If any required provenance field is missing, the external result is `unknown` with a machine-readable `missing_provenance` reason and no partial deploy object. The code does not consult internal room metadata or inferred ownership; negative tests cover each missing field, authorization still runs before lookup,"]}]},{"id":"f8a13ec1-a15b-801e-8f49-b0c763d72dbe","rank":22,"occurredAt":"2023-10-05T15:18:00Z","content":"Iris sent a small Lantern copy pass before a Product Engineering feedback session. This is only for the narrow internal-adoption cleanup, not a scope change, and I want the empty-state language to preserve the actual v0 boundaries. We should not imply an owner when the owner-map source lacks provenance, we should not make a health/readiness claim when deploy movement is absent from permissioned sources, and we should not surface raw incident text. Can you choose or rewrite the copy so each line is short, user-facing, and explicit about provenance and permissions without sounding broken or defensive?","artifact":{"id":"d565218f-11c8-4a67-9133-5bd90f9968ad","kind":"source","occurredAt":"2023-10-05T15:18:00Z"},"sources":[{"sourceId":"alex-000583","occurredAt":"2023-10-05T15:18:00Z","metadata":{"role":"user","author":"Alex Valdez","localTime":"2023-10-05T11:18:00-04:00"},"label":"Alex Valdez, message 000583","excerpts":[]}]},{"id":"29a01175-45e0-896f-aec0-dd0686106fbe","rank":23,"occurredAt":"2023-08-01T13:20:00Z","content":"We have a more specific Lantern provenance split now. Roman found that the rollup-service ownership row does have an audit-note source reference from the May 22 owner-map work; the import just failed to carry it into Lantern's provenance field. Nadia found a worse case for alerting/dashboards: the current row is true, but the only available reference right now is a Slack message, not the audit-style source Lantern expects. Iris asked whether v0 can render rollup-service after the source_ref import fix while continuing to omit alerting/dashboards until Nadia has proper recorded provenance. I think yes. Write a clear reply that says exactly that, and explicitly says the omission does not challenge Nadia's ownership in the owner map.","artifact":{"id":"e97e078c-0e03-4924-a365-10236ce72bf9","kind":"source","occurredAt":"2023-08-01T13:20:00Z"},"sources":[{"sourceId":"alex-000366","occurredAt":"2023-08-01